	GDLLMTunables.DEBUG_GAME_MAX_STEPS: "The most step presses one debug_game call may make; the result traces where each press landed, and the tool's description quotes the live value. Each press can wait several seconds for the break to land on a slow game, so the ceiling stays modest and the whole call is additionally bounded by the step budget below — the model can always call debug_game again for more steps.",
	GDLLMTunables.DEBUG_GAME_STEP_BUDGET_MS: "One debug_game call's whole wall-clock stepping budget (in milliseconds) — the debug counterpart to suspend_game's step budget. When stepping exceeds it, the call stops and reports the presses that landed and where the game stands, rather than holding the conversation while a slow game grinds through the rest.",
